WEBVTT

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.240
With this, you are finished!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.210
You’ve died five times now!
All in this puzzle I’ve crafted!

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:32.410
Who is it?!

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.680
Who dares to interrupt
my moment of bliss?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.970
You have my apologies.
Should I call back later?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.470
Aren’t you...?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.230
I’ve greatly enjoyed reviewing
the puzzles you’ve sent me.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.400
These puzzles are clearly overflowing
with brilliance and zeal.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.400
I haven’t been this
impressed in some time.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.990
Allow me to jump straight to the point.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.660
Me, become a Master Brain?!

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.250
Is there a problem?

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.300
Hey, what’s gotten into you?

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.180
My apologies. I haven’t had an
evening this amusing in ages!

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.640
Would you mind if I interpreted
that as a good thing?

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.520
Depending on the conditions,
I might be willing to lend you a hand.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.800
Just you wait, Kaito Daimon!

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.030
I, Herbert Mueller, am sure to defeat
you with this next puzzle!

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.990
Is That What You Thought I’d Say?

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.010
Huh?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.590
Eh?!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.590
Like this?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:23.930
How’s it go?

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.350
Like this?
How’s it go?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.010
Like this?
That’s not right...

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:25.850
Sheesh...

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.640
Huh?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.060
Here?
Over there... That’s open.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.220
Isn’t that off?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.650
Jeez! We come to South America
and you’re at another puzzle?

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.980
No, duh! It’s not
like we came to play!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.820
Sure, I know this isn’t fun and games.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.110
But there’s the Machu
Picchu, Geoglyphs of Nazca,

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.620
Pampas de Jumana, the ruins at Chavin
de Hauntar, and bunch of rare sights!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.370
I wanna go! Man, I wanna see them!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.120
Let it drop.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.880
<i>She doesn’t see why we are here.</i>

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.500
Hey, Q-taro! Are you sure
there’s a Puzzle of Fools?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.760
According to that Master Brain’s hint,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.930
it should be somewhere around here...

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.970
<i>You should say so with
confidence, Doctor.</i>

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.640
It looks way cooler
facing this direction!

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.940
That’s the entrance!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.690
Ana, you’re incredible!

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.560
This is...

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.510
Alpaca!

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.720
Is this... the puzzle?

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.180
Looks like the Master
Brain ain’t around!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.190
The door leadin’ to
the next room is locked!

00:04:59.190 --> 00:04:59.990
Kaito!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.570
Look!

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.450
That’s--!

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.450
Its the ring she wore
back that one time!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.960
Yeah. Now we know for
sure: Raetsel was here.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.340
This Philosopher’s
Puzzle was another dud.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.760
Where in the world could the
Pythagoras Document be?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.970
It looks like we’ll have no choice
but to check those ruins.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:37.140
But, Master Rook,
even according to the POG’s charters,

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.310
it is taboo to so much
as step foot in there.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.320
Yeah, but something
about it smells fishy.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.800
“Pythagoras’ Ruins.”

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.100
I’m sure we’ll find
something inside...

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.830
Here are the rules for this puzzle:

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.750
We must correctly place the
pieces on the center pedestal.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.500
However, we’re only given one
chance to move the pieces.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.510
We must pick up and set down
the pieces at the same time.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.890
The bases for these eight alpaca
statues are the “pieces.”

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.930
If you look at them from above,
they’re all quadrilaterals.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:18.310
And these five are the only ones
that fit inside perfectly.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.730
Is everyone ready?

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.400
Gammon
I’m cool!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.860
I wish I brought Iwashimizu with us!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.860
Iwarin was saying,
“Must rest and recuperate.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.060
Rest time! Rest time!”

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.040
Whatever! Just hurry
and get this over with!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.700
We’ve gotta put these
down at the same time.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:37.750
And now!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.750
Are you okay?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.170
Hey! Why was the platform under
me the only one that tilted?!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.720
Open Sesame!

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.620
Sweet! That was the right answer.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.460
Let’s go.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.220
What’s with this room?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.770
Kaito Daimon and your crew,
I was growing weary of waiting!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.960
Thrice I have returned,

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.800
all to settle the score that has
grown to massive proportions!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.340
Herbert!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.930
What’re you doin’ here?!

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:36.680
I have taken the time to come
dispose of you personally.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.390
I’m here as the Republic
of Amgine’s Head of

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.560
Puzzles and Special Assistant to the President!

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.940
As the Special Assistant
to the President?!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.820
Meaning you’re a Master Brain?!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.820
I’m not here to see you!
Where are Jin and Raetsel?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:59.120
I’m willing to tell you, but only if
you manage to free my puzzle.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:02.210
You aren’t my enemy!
Just tell me where they are!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.710
I see you are taking me lightly.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:09.050
However, I am no longer the
same man you once knew!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.460
Allow me to show you...

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.220
...how I have been reborn anew!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.310
Replica Rings?!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.600
You’re still wearing those?!

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.480
Didn’t the POG recover all of them...?

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.520
I am currently the only person

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.050
in the world with possession
of these Rings!

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.860
And on top of these...!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.490
You put on more?!

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.160
The more Rings, the better.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.450
I can think clearly!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.600
I have become the first person in

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:46.380
human history to rule over four Rings!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.410
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.760
Those things put incredible
strain on your mind!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.140
I am the Angel of Vengeance,
sent to do Heaven’s bidding!

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.760
Such concerns mean nothing to me!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.740
You shall suffer humiliation

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.830
and despair in retribution
for trying to take my life!

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.860
We tried to kill you?

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.530
You’re the one who’s always
throwing us into harm’s way!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.650
And Nonoha saved you that last time...

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.060
Silence!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.370
Feast your eyes on this!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:33.630
Detestable Phi-Brain children,
pit yourselves against my puzzle.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:36.510
There you shall find five balances.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.550
Each of you must identify your own bag

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.140
before inputting the correct answer
into the central puzzle!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.890
Our own bag?

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.270
I took the liberty of
weighing you earlier.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.570
Y-you weighed me without asking?!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.860
You are not allowed to touch the bag.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.870
You may use the balances
up to ten times.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.530
For your first shot at
it, all five of you are

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.680
to stand on the balances simultaneously.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.580
I am giving you ten minutes.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.170
If you cannot reach the correct
answer within the time limit,

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.980
the Blocks of Judgment shall rain
upon you from the heavens.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.590
You shall pay for your
sins with your very lives.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.180
You’re a scumball for weighing a girl!

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.000
But if we don’t solve this,

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.500
we won’t learn about Raetsel’s puzzle...

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.600
Kaito, we don’t have
to solve this puzzle.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:29.880
We do!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.980
He’s been possessed by the Rings.
I can’t just leave him!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:38.280
The four Rings are forcibly
stimulating his brain!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.490
If we don’t stop them
soon, they could kill him!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:43.950
I see...

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.250
Are you ready to depart
for your journey to Hell?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.250
You’re on! I’ll
accept your challenge.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.560
It’s puzzle time... Let’s start!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.580
For starters, we’ll never solve this

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.350
if we don’t know everyone’s weights.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:11.850
I’m 60kg.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.360
I, Ana, am 47!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:14.860
I’m 40kg.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.860
I’m 78. That makes me the heaviest.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.450
I’m a mere 30kg!

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.370
Kidding! I’m between Kaito and Ana...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.370
We’ve got all the info we need, right?

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.660
Then we can solve the puzzle now.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.170
Let’s do it!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.510
Ready, go!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.010
We didn’t get any lucky matches, huh?

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.510
But we found out where my bag is.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.480
We did?

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:47.100
Yeah.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:52.600
Goin’ from lightest to heaviest,
it’s Cubik, Ana, Nonoha, Kaito and then me.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.110
The bag on Kaito’s balance
was heavier than him.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.940
So I’m the only person
it could match up with.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.530
Oh, that makes sense!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:04.030
We get five more tries at the balances.
This’ll be a piece of cake.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:05.480
Oomph!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.520
We can take it one person
at a time from here on out.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.540
You’re next, Ana. Get
on this yellow balance.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:12.410
Sure thing!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.040
What’s the matter, Kaito?

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.210
Nah, it’s nothing.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.030
Something’s off. At most, we’ll use

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:30.230
the balances eight times
before reaching the answer.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:34.060
Darn it, Herbert! Are you keeping
something from us again?

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:42.070
Kaito Daimon’s life will draw to
an end before much longer.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.070
Excellent. You are meeting
my expectations, Herbert.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.080
Now then, about what we had discussed.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:55.580
I know. You are worthy of someday
leading the Republic of Amgine.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.590
If you should win, I will start by

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.300
transferring command over all
of the Master Brains to you.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.090
I have your word on that?

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.660
But of course.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.100
I’m awaiting your favorable report.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:15.920
That one’s lighter than Ana.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.980
In that case, that bag has
to match up with Cubik.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.150
I’m next!

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:24.740
Wha--?!

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.570
What the hell?!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.460
Eh? What? What’s the big deal?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.330
That result’s impossible!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.200
Two of the bags are heavier than Kaito.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.620
What?!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.080
Gammon is the only person
here heavier than Kaito,

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.830
but two bags meet that criteria.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.590
Which means...

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.090
You’re up to your stinkin’ cheap tricks again,
aren’t you?! Herbert!

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.840
“Cheap”? So what of it?

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.720
Doesn’t Jin Makata
encourage such behavior?

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.100
He says, “Do whatever
it takes to win.”

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.850
What was that?!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:01.070
Animosity can fuel a person’s heart.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.230
At times, it can serve
as fodder for power.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.240
How truly fascinating.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.660
How are we supposed
to answer this if you

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.500
screwed with the weight of the bags?!

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.250
I’ve presented all of
the necessary information.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.000
If you can’t solve it, then you have
your own stupidity to blame.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.010
Sounds fun!

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.260
What?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.080
You may not play fair, but you never

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.160
present puzzles that
don’t have answers.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.370
That’s the one thing I
about you I can count on.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.390
Just you watch.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:39.440
There is no puzzle I cannot solve!

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:43.780
Only the first balances
moved differently.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.990
There must have been a reason for that.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.290
Our weights...

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.090
We were convinced that
it was our body weight,

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.040
but that was Herbert’s trap.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.790
There was an alpaca statue by my
feet when Herbert weighed us.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:06.130
Inversely, Nonoha should be
lighter since the floor sank.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.010
I’ve got it!

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.010
Ana, get on the red balance!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:11.890
Huh?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.510
No time to explain! Hurry!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:14.300
Roger!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.100
He’s figured it out? Curse you!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.440
Moron! What’s wrong with you?!

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.180
As the Giver, I get to decide the rules.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.190
There aren’t any puzzles that
you can’t solve, right?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:35.240
The red balance is lighter than Nonoha,
but heavier than Ana.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.950
So that bag goes to Nonoha!

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.210
In that case, the remaining
balance goes to...

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.080
Ana, get on that one!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:44.920
Okay!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.010
Whoosh!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.190
Perfect!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.220
I’ve solved it!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.070
And that’s a wrap!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.130
Nice!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.550
Why must I lose?

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:40.220
How... and where did I go wrong?

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.980
Tell me: Where is Jin?

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.240
He isn’t here.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.230
He should be in the Andes at present.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.650
You better not be feedin’ us bull!

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:57.150
At the moment, I have no
reason to deceive you.

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:02.300
Fair enough. Then there’s nothing
left to keep us here.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.570
Let’s get goin’, Kaito.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:05.990
Herbert!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:12.510
Sure enough, I just can’t bring
myself to hate your puzzles.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.510
In that case, I shall make
a puzzle that will vex you,

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:22.020
make you stamp your feet in frustration.

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.020
What you said back then...

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.520
I think those words reflected
how you truly feel inside.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.030
Quit wearing those Rings and
being so damn stubborn!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.030
Get rid of those things!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.950
And then show it to me--Let
me see your true puzzle!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.160
My true puzzle?!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:44.540
I haven’t given you all I have?!
Is that what you’re saying?!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.170
How badly must you disgrace
me before you’re satisfied?!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:53.170
Stop it! Don’t use the
Rings powers anymore!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:59.640
I’ll do whatever it takes to send you
to the pit of hell, Kaito Daimon!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.390
There was no reason for me to have lost.

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.570
So where did I go wrong?!

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.800
You lost because of your foul trickery.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.570
Wha--?!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.780
Didn’t you say that you would
face him fair-and-square?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.410
Why didn’t you keep your word?

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.160
Well, you see...

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.680
Don’t be stupid!

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.670
You shoulda made a puzzle
so cheap that no one coulda solved it!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:27.580
A-another one?!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.620
I’m totally screwed! It’s
all over; I’m finished!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.140
I see. These must be creating you!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.840
Why won’t they come off?!

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.070
Are even the Rings making a fool of me?

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:57.110
You’re eyesores! You,
these Rings, everything!

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.250
Don’t appear before me ever again!

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:01.570
Disappear...

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:06.250
...for all eternity!

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:16.050
The Rings...

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:20.300
What... just happened?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.140
The Rings came off!

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:28.800
Are you okay, Herbert?

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:34.190
I see... So it was all a nightmare.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:41.200
You have my gratitude,
Kaito Daimon and crew.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:44.070
I was clearly in the wrong.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:48.580
I shall put all of the grudges
I’ve held against you behind me.

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.340
Herbert...

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.820
And next time, let’s pit
our skills against each

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.430
other on the ultimate puzzle as friendly rivals.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.120
Is that what you thought I’d say?

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.510
Punk!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:08.310
The whole lot of you can
go to hell together!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.060
Stupid! You’re the one standing
under the trap right now!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.100
What?!

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:19.740
Herbert!

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:27.740
Please save me!

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.080
That was the worst puzzle
in all of history!

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:37.500
It tells you my weight!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.920
<i>Herbert weighs 80 kilograms.</i>

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:41.970
The Andes, huh?

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:47.180
I analyzed him and anything
he says has zero reliability!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.260
<i>It’s zero!</i>

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.100
But Her-Her wasn’t lying to us.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.520
He isn’t here.

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.850
He should be in the Andes at present.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.110
Doesn’t matter either
way ya look at it.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.270
A Master Brain’s waiting for
us at our next destination.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.610
What makes you so certain?

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.520
She’s luring us out with the prize

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:07.620
and waiting for her prey
to fall for the trap.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.120
That’s the way the puzzle
Raetsel made works.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:13.140
Sounds convincing.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:16.880
The prize is Jin Makata and the
traps are the Master Brains, right?

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.490
That ring is nothin’ more than bait.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.380
We’re already caught in her trap.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:23.630
All over a measly ring...

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:24.430
<i>Smooth!</i>

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.470
Raetsel...

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.340
I’m so happy!

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:38.360
I’m thrilled that I get
to travel with you again, Jin.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:49.700
Raetsel, you’re free
to abandon puzzles.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:54.710
But she’s missing something.
That’s the feeling I get.

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.460
Perhaps the two are connected.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:03.840
If Jin’s memories come back,
he’ll abandon me again...

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:07.470
Is something wrong?

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.720
Nuh-huh. It’s nothing.

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:15.190
It’s getting cold. Why
don’t we head on back?

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:16.760
Uh-huh.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:23.980
I won’t let him take Jin.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:28.560
Before he can, I’ll deal with
Kaito Daimon myself...

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:04.710
Hello. Freecell?

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:06.590
Um, who is this?

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:07.960
It’s me! Me!

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:09.420
That’s not terribly helpful...

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:11.630
You know? I’m with the POG.

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:12.720
Mr. Bishop?

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:14.260
No. I’m the one with a ball of hair.

00:24:14.260 --> 00:24:15.970
Oh, Funga!

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:17.010
He has an afro.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:18.680
I’ve got it! You’re Herbert.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.600
His time to shine is over.

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:27.970
She’s Too Shallow

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:23.310
Next time, “She’s Too Shallow.”

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:24.980
I give. I have no idea who you are.

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:27.280
You’re just yanking
my chain, aren’t you?

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
One for all!
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
